WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.220
MARTIN OMANDER: Li Na
sent me a question--

00:00:02.220 --> 00:00:05.070
how do I authenticate calls
to my Cloud Run service?

00:00:05.070 --> 00:00:06.720
Well, it depends.

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:09.180
One, if your service
is a web or mobile app

00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:11.430
backend and you need
to validate the user,

00:00:11.430 --> 00:00:13.770
use Firebase
Authentication, send the JWT

00:00:13.770 --> 00:00:15.540
token from your
client, and validate it

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:17.340
in your Cloud Run service.

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:19.530
Two, if your service
is a backend,

00:00:19.530 --> 00:00:22.590
but you don't want to validate
the JWT token in your code,

00:00:22.590 --> 00:00:24.510
consider API Gateway.

00:00:24.510 --> 00:00:26.460
Three, if your
service should only

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:29.400
be reachable from other services
in your Google Cloud project,

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:32.549
set Ingress to allow
internal traffic only.

00:00:32.549 --> 00:00:34.500
Four, if your
service should only

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:36.330
be reachable from
other services, which

00:00:36.330 --> 00:00:39.450
may run outside Google
Cloud, download a key file

00:00:39.450 --> 00:00:42.600
from Google Cloud and set
Require Authentication.

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:44.550
Five, if your
service should only

00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:47.580
be reachable by people
in your organization,

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:51.270
set up a load balancer, Identity
Aware Proxy, and set Ingress

00:00:51.270 --> 00:00:52.470
accordingly.

00:00:52.470 --> 00:00:55.240
What are your Google Cloud
Serverless questions?

00:00:55.240 --> 00:00:57.290
Post them in the comments.

